From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:20:40 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add CBM core - registers, buffer pools, FSQM

Start the CBM (Central Buffer Manager, the GRX500 "CQM" complex)
support with its foundations:

 - cbm.h and cbm_regs.h hold the byte-exact structure layouts and
   the register topology of the eleven CBM MMIO windows (EQM enqueue
   manager, DQM dequeue manager, FSQM free-segment queue manager,
   load spreader, descriptor windows, TMU), and the port vocabulary
   the manager speaks, meaning the dequeue-resource structures and the
   port-class flags it fills in.

 - cbm_buf.c serves the packet-buffer pools. The standard (18 MiB) and
   jumbo (8 MiB) pools are no-map reserved-memory carve-outs the
   board device tree declares, looked up by their memory-region names
   std-pool and jumbo-pool and mapped with memremap. Pool physical
   bases feed both the FSQM seeding and the SBA/JBA base registers.

 - fsqm.c: FSQM initialization - seed the linked-list table
   (LLT_RAM) with the per-slot reference counts, program the
   OFSQ/OFSC/LSARNG free-queue geometry and FSQT thresholds,
   enable interrupts, and only then set CTRL=1. The vendor
   ordering (drain the IO_BUF, arm CTRL last) is load-bearing:
   arming the FSQM before the rest of the geometry is programmed
   corrupts the free-segment accounting.

 - cbm_basic.c holds word-wise MMIO helpers.

The arrays indexed by datapath port are sized for the full 0..15 space,
because the TX descriptor's endpoint field is 4 bits wide and 15 is the
largest datapath port the hardware can express.

Nothing builds this code yet. The buffer manager, the traffic manager
and the DMA driver resolve symbols against each other, so they are wired
into the build together once the last of them exists.

Structure layouts and register sequences derived from the AVM FRITZ!Box
7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198), cqm/grx500/ (cbm.c, cbm.h, the
generated reg/*.h). Those vendor sources carry no copyright notice of
their own, in that release or in any other checked, so there is none to
preserve and none is invented: each file header names the vendor file it
came from instead.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

